Relationship to opencode
------------------------
Captain Code drives worker sessions through opencode (https://opencode.ai,
sst/opencode, MIT) by spawning `opencode serve` and speaking to its HTTP API.
No opencode source code is included in or derived from this repository; it is
an external program this one talks to, the same way it talks to `claude`,
`codex` and `cursor-agent`.

The terminal-side integration that lets an opencode TUI route its prompts
through Captain Code is maintained separately, as a patch series against
upstream opencode, and carries opencode's own copyright and MIT license:

  sst/opencode - Copyright (c) 2025 opencode, MIT License

Third-party services
--------------------
Model providers reached through this software are governed by their own terms.
Captain Code holds no credentials of its own: it uses the credentials present
on the machine it runs on.
